    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. is there anything else it could be besides the belt? like could it be something more electrical or just some random mechanical failure in the accessories itself?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While the belt is a prime suspect, you are right to consider other possibilities, as the squealing could be coming from the accessories themselves, not just the belt slipping. It's quite common for a failing pulley bearing on one of the accessories—like the alternator or the water pump—to make a high-pitched whine or squeal when the engine loads up, which happens when you press the gas. It's less likely to be purely electrical, but a seized or struggling accessory can put too much strain on the belt, causing the noise. A good mechanic will check the tension and condition of the belt *and* inspect the bearings of all the pulleys.",
      "source": "target",
