    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "ok so if it is a pulley or a bearing, how do i know which one it is? is there a way to tell if it's just a random, weird glitch in the system or if it's definitely a physical part breaking?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Determining the exact source of the squeal without tools is tricky, but you can try to narrow it down by listening carefully when the noise occurs. If the squeal changes pitch or volume significantly when you turn the steering wheel, the power steering pump is a strong candidate. If it sounds more consistent and high-pitched under acceleration, it often points toward the alternator or an idler pulley bearing. A physical part breaking, like a bearing seizing up, usually produces a grinding or a very distinct, constant whine rather than just a simple squeak.",
